{"batchcomplete":"","continue":{"gsroffset":8,"continue":"gsroffset||"},"query":{"pages":{"92403889":{"pageid":92403889,"ns":6,"title":"File:Environmental acoustic considerations for passive detection of maritime targets by hydrophones in a deep ocean trench (IA environmentalcou109455301).pdf","index":5,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":2327112,"width":1275,"height":1650,"pagecount":82,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Environmental_acoustic_considerations_for_passive_detection_of_maritime_targets_by_hydrophones_in_a_deep_ocean_trench_%28IA_environmentalcou109455301%29.pdf/page1-960px-Environmental_acoustic_considerations_for_passive_detection_of_maritime_targets_by_hydrophones_in_a_deep_ocean_trench_%28IA_environmentalcou109455301%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1800,"thumbheight":2329,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Environmental_acoustic_considerations_for_passive_detection_of_maritime_targets_by_hydrophones_in_a_deep_ocean_trench_%28IA_environmentalcou109455301%29.pdf/page1-960px-Environmental_acoustic_considerations_for_passive_detection_of_maritime_targets_by_hydrophones_in_a_deep_ocean_trench_%28IA_environmentalcou109455301%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1800,"height":2329},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/49/Environmental_acoustic_considerations_for_passive_detection_of_maritime_targets_by_hydrophones_in_a_deep_ocean_trench_%28IA_environmentalcou109455301%29.pdf?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Environmental_acoustic_considerations_for_passive_detection_of_maritime_targets_by_hydrophones_in_a_deep_ocean_trench_(IA_environmentalcou109455301).pdf","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=92403889","extmetadata":{"Artist":{"value":"<div class=\"fn value\">\nBiediger, Jeremy S.</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<div class=\"description\">\n<p>This thesis explores the potential advantage of deep ocean trench placement of an acoustic sensor network. The hypothesis is that a hydrophone deployed in a deep ocean trench will operate in an environment of reduced ambient noise such that passive maritime surveillance may be performed with relatively high signal-to-noise ratio (SNR). Barrier or \\\"tripwire\\\" coverage along the oceanic trench is made possible by virtue of networked acoustic communication among widely spaced hydrophones. Physics-based hydro-acoustic propagation modeling supports analysis of target-to-sensor propagation and networked acoustic communication links in representative trench environments.\n</p>\n<br>Subjects: Underwater acoustics; Submarine trenches; Anti-submarine warfare</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"201822328":{"pageid":201822328,"ns":6,"title":"File:FK151121 - Hydrothermal Hunt on the Mariana Back-arc.pdf","index":4,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":23246676,"width":1275,"height":1650,"pagecount":107,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/FK151121_-_Hydrothermal_Hunt_on_the_Mariana_Back-arc.pdf/page1-960px-FK151121_-_Hydrothermal_Hunt_on_the_Mariana_Back-arc.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1800,"thumbheight":2329,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/FK151121_-_Hydrothermal_Hunt_on_the_Mariana_Back-arc.pdf/page1-960px-FK151121_-_Hydrothermal_Hunt_on_the_Mariana_Back-arc.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1800,"height":2329},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/28/FK151121_-_Hydrothermal_Hunt_on_the_Mariana_Back-arc.pdf?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FK151121_-_Hydrothermal_Hunt_on_the_Mariana_Back-arc.pdf","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=201822328","extmetadata":{"Artist":{"value":"<div class=\"fn value\">\nSusan Merle and William Chadwick</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"99934803":{"pageid":99934803,"ns":6,"title":"File:Fmars-08-642040.pdf","index":8,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":4360403,"width":1239,"height":1622,"pagecount":11,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Fmars-08-642040.pdf/page1-960px-Fmars-08-642040.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1800,"thumbheight":2356,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Fmars-08-642040.pdf/page1-960px-Fmars-08-642040.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1800,"height":2356},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0a/Fmars-08-642040.pdf?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fmars-08-642040.pdf","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=99934803","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"The seafloor beneath floating ice shelves accounts roughly a third of the Antarctic\u2019s 5 million km2 of continental shelf. Prior to this study, our knowledge of these habitats and the life they support was restricted to what has been observed from eight boreholes drilled for geological and glaciological studies. The established theory of sub-ice shelf biogeography is that both functional and taxonomic diversities decrease along a nutrient gradient with distance from the ice shelf front, resulting in a depauperate fauna, dominated by mobile scavengers and predators toward the grounding line. Mobile macro-benthic life and mega-benthic life have been observed as far as 700 km under an ice shelf. New observations from two boreholes in the Filchner-Ronne Ice Shelf challenge the idea that sessile organisms reduce in prevalence the further under the ice you go. The discovery of an established community consisting of only sessile, probably filter feeding, organisms (sponges and other taxa) on a boulder 260 km from the ice front raises significant questions, especially when the local currents suggest that this community is somewhere between 625 km and 1500 km in the direction of water flow from the nearest region of photosynthesis. This new evidence requires us to rethink our ideas with regard to the diversity of community types found under ice shelves, the key factors which control their distribution and their vulnerability to environmental change and ice shelf collapse.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2021-02-15","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"Huw J. Griffiths, Paul Anker, Katrin Linse, Jamie Maxwell, Alexandra L. Post, Craig Stevens, Slawek Tulaczyk and James A. Smith","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"105462507":{"pageid":105462507,"ns":6,"title":"File:GEBCO 2019 bathymetry Challenger Deep and Sirena Deep.jpg","index":3,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":996418,"width":2128,"height":1552,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/GEBCO_2019_bathymetry_Challenger_Deep_and_Sirena_Deep.jpg/1920px-GEBCO_2019_bathymetry_Challenger_Deep_and_Sirena_Deep.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1800,"thumbheight":1313,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/26/GEBCO_2019_bathymetry_Challenger_Deep_and_Sirena_Deep.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/GEBCO_2019_bathymetry_Challenger_Deep_and_Sirena_Deep.jpg/1920px-GEBCO_2019_bathymetry_Challenger_Deep_and_Sirena_Deep.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1800,"height":1313,"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/26/GEBCO_2019_bathymetry_Challenger_Deep_and_Sirena_Deep.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/26/GEBCO_2019_bathymetry_Challenger_Deep_and_Sirena_Deep.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GEBCO_2019_bathymetry_Challenger_Deep_and_Sirena_Deep.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=105462507","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"GEBCO 2019 bathymetry of the Challenger Deep and the Sirena Deep.<br>\n<p>(a) Mariana Trench multibeam bathymetry data gridded at 75 m acquired on\u2010board the DSSV Pressure Drop overtop the GEBCO 2019 source grid (as shown in Figure 1) and the complete GEBCO 2019 grid with hillshade. EM 124 black contours at 500 m intervals, GEBCO 2019 grey contours at 1,000 m intervals. The white circle indicates the deepest point and submersible dive location, the white triangle indicates the submersible dive location from Sirena Deep, the red spot was the deepest point derived by van Haren et al., (2017).<br>\n(b) Challenger Deep.<br>\n(c) Sirena Deep.<br>\n</p>\nBathymetric cross sections A\u2019\u2013A\u201d and B\u2019\u2013B\u201d over Challenger Deep and Sirena Deep displayed in (d) and (e), respectively.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2021-05-18","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"Cassandra Bongiovanni, Heather A. Stewart and Alan J. Jamieson","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"156917940":{"pageid":156917940,"ns":6,"title":"File:Map of the Mariana Trench- Bathymetry QGIS 3 0 (M\u00e9diHAL 1991387).pdf","index":1,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":908653,"width":1752,"height":1239,"pagecount":1,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Map_of_the_Mariana_Trench-_Bathymetry_QGIS_3_0_%28M%C3%A9diHAL_1991387%29.pdf/page1-1280px-Map_of_the_Mariana_Trench-_Bathymetry_QGIS_3_0_%28M%C3%A9diHAL_1991387%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1800,"thumbheight":1273,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Map_of_the_Mariana_Trench-_Bathymetry_QGIS_3_0_%28M%C3%A9diHAL_1991387%29.pdf/page1-1280px-Map_of_the_Mariana_Trench-_Bathymetry_QGIS_3_0_%28M%C3%A9diHAL_1991387%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1800,"height":1273},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b2/Map_of_the_Mariana_Trench-_Bathymetry_QGIS_3_0_%28M%C3%A9diHAL_1991387%29.pdf?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Mariana_Trench-_Bathymetry_QGIS_3_0_(M%C3%A9diHAL_1991387).pdf","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=156917940","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Polina Lemenkova. Map of the Mariana Trench: Bathymetry. QGIS 3.0. Qingdao, China. 2018. \u27e8medihal-01991387\u27e9","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateT